#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / base-files Specification
PACKAGE: base-files
LANGUAGE: Shell, packaging data, native integration as upstream defines
STATUS: W1
ROLE: Fundamental filesystem identity, release metadata, baseline system files

## PROGRAM
base-files establishes essential filesystem content and release identity used by the operating system.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Ubuntu/Debian package
BOUNDARY: package data -> filesystem identity -> release metadata
WHITE_EDITION: identity/documentation overlay

## SPEC
- preserve standard filesystem semantics
- identify White Edition separately from upstream version
- keep ownership and permissions deterministic
- document White Edition paths explicitly

## QUALITY
TEST: package build, filesystem layout, ownership, permissions, metadata, upgrade compatibility

## SOURCE POLICY
Prefer package data and packaging changes. Native source changes require a demonstrated requirement and regression evidence.
